@flexiarg snatch/a-free-mark-is-always-worth-assigning
@title A Free Mark Is Always Worth Assigning
@audience players
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/mark-without-force

! conclusion: When a mark costs nothing now and is visible later, assign it.

  + context: **Play grain.** Snatch or Share under G3, immediately after a snatch,
    where P1 may assign a shame token and no tokens move either way.

  + IF:
    You may attach a durable, visible mark to a counterpart who defected, and
    assigning it changes no payoff in the current round.

  + HOWEVER:
    It is easy to read *"changes nothing now"* as *"changes nothing"*, and a
    player optimising the round will decline a move with no immediate return.

  + THEN:
    Assign it, and treat declining as the decision it is — one that must be
    justified, not a default.

  + BECAUSE:
    The mark is free at the moment it is cheapest to make and priced at every
    later round in which it is visible. Declining spends a future deterrent to
    save nothing.
